{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.FigureEightTriangulation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightTriangulation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation","lean:module:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightTri.edge_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightTri.edge_one","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightTriangulation.lean#L134-L140","doc":"**Edge 1**: `(1/(1−w)) · (1 − 1/w)² ` squared `= 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightTri.edge_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightTri.edge_zero","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightTriangulation.lean#L128-L132","doc":"**Edge 0**: `w⁴ · (1/(1−w))² = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightTri.figureEightTriangulation_volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightTri.figureEightTriangulation_volume","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightTriangulation.lean#L107-L119","doc":"**`volume (4₁ triangulation) = VOL_4_1`.**\n\nDirect from `blochWigner_lob_exp`: the shape is on the unit circle, so its volume\nis `Cl₂(π/3)` with no further work, and there are two of them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightTri.regularTet_angle₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightTri.regularTet_angle₁","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightTriangulation.lean#L100-L105","doc":"All three dihedral angles of the regular tetrahedron are `π/3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightTri.figureEightTriangulation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightTri.figureEightTriangulation","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightTriangulation.lean#L96-L98","doc":"**The 4₁ ideal triangulation**: two regular tetrahedra, per SnapPy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightTri.regularTet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightTri.regularTet","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightTriangulation.lean#L93-L94","doc":"The regular ideal tetrahedron. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightTri.one_sub_w_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightTri.one_sub_w_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightTriangulation.lean#L88-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightTri.w_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightTri.w_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightTriangulation.lean#L86-L86","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightTri.w_sq_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightTri.w_sq_sub","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightTriangulation.lean#L79-L84","doc":"**The minimal polynomial**: `w² − w + 1 = 0`, so the shape field is `ℚ(√−3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightTri.w_add_one_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightTri.w_add_one_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightTriangulation.lean#L71-L77","doc":"`w + 1 ≠ 0`.  Note `w = −1` *does* satisfy `w³ = −1`, so the cube alone does\nnot rule it out — the imaginary part does. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightTri.w_im_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightTri.w_im_pos","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightTriangulation.lean#L64-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightTri.w_cube","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightTri.w_cube","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightTriangulation.lean#L56-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightTri.w","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightTri.w","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightTriangulation.lean#L53-L54","doc":"The regular ideal tetrahedron's shape, `e^{iπ/3}`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}